<title>CANADA: DBRS downgrades Canadian Occidental debt.</title>
<headline>DBRS downgrades Canadian Occidental debt.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dominion Bond Rating Service Ltd said on Tuesday it downgraded Canadian Occidental Petroleum Ltd's long-term debt and confirmed its rating of the company's commercial paper after CanOxy's C$2 billion takeover of Wascana Energy Inc.</p>
<p>DBRS also said it confirmed Wascana's long-term debt rating.</p>
<p>CanOxy's long-term unsecured debt was downgraded to A (low) from A and its commercial paper was confirmed at R-1 (low), DBRS said. The outlook on the securities was rated as stable.  </p>
<p>DBRS said that CanOxy's debt levels would rise sharply and, despite strong cash flow from expanding production, the risk element in the long term debt had risen.</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
